session:
  updated: 2026-07-26
  status: validation_complete
  branch: main

goal:
  current: diagnose and fix agent cold-start misses of AGENTS.md in generated projects

completed:
  - added `## Session startup` near the top of `AGENTS.md`
  - added required session startup section 1 to `.agentic-template/templates/AGENTS_TEMPLATE.md`
  - tightened README onboarding to require reading `AGENTS.md` from disk and confirming it
  - tightened `.github/copilot-instructions.md` as an external agent startup surface
  - diagnosed the chicken-and-egg gap as missing cold-start adapters and no executable startup handshake outside `AGENTS.md`
  - added `.agentic-template/bin/project startup` to print `AGENTS.md` from disk and list follow-on state files
  - added an ASCII startup welcome, boot sequence and options menu to `project startup`
  - added a Claude native skill adapter at `.claude/skills/agentic-template/SKILL.md`
  - added a Cursor always-applied project rule at `.cursor/rules/agentic-startup-and-skills.mdc`
  - tightened `.codex/README.md` and `.claude/README.md` to require startup or disk-read confirmation
  - made generated READMEs require an `Agent startup` section with `.agentic-template/bin/project startup`
  - fixed `check-wiki` dirty-tree drift detection so uncommitted wiki updates count as local documentation updates
  - updated `check-repo-contract` to require the startup section, disk-read language and pre-identity placement
  - added self-test regressions for missing live, template, README, Claude, Codex, Cursor and Copilot startup rules and startup display
  - captured `INBOX-007` for the reusable startup disk-read contract pattern

in_progress: []

next:
  - use the startup rule in the next generated project and promote `INBOX-007` if it reduces startup contract misses

decisions:
  - id: structured_data_policy_configurable
    summary: generated projects can choose TOON or S-expressions by purpose; template control files remain TOON until tooling is specialised
  - id: context_packet_for_delegation
    summary: context-window pressure is handled through semantic packets with source refs, not byte-compressed or opaque prompt payloads
  - id: generated_readme_low_clutter
    summary: generated READMEs should stay project-facing; template operating detail belongs in AGENTS, docs map, profile and hidden template docs unless directly useful
  - id: knowledge_upkeep_handoff_gate
    summary: meaningful work must record consulted knowledge, proposals created or a concrete no-record rationale
  - id: read_only_status_commands
    summary: backlog and worktree status commands expose coordination state without merge or cleanup automation
  - id: conditional_runbooks
    summary: runbook scaffolding exists, but concrete runbooks are added only for repeated operations with evidence
  - id: session_startup_disk_read
    summary: agents must read `AGENTS.md` from disk before substantive answers or tool calls; `project startup`, generated templates and supported agent entrypoints repeat the rule
  - id: thin_native_agent_adapters
    summary: Claude and Cursor get native startup/skill-routing adapters that point back to `.agents/skills/CATALOG.toon` instead of duplicating the canonical skill tree

risks:
  - check-handoff validates knowledge bookkeeping structurally but does not prove semantic freshness
  - check-wiki remains warn-only; human or lead agent must still promote useful inbox entries after evidence
  - worktree-status reports observable git state and does not reconcile mismatches automatically
  - repository checks can enforce startup contract wording and adapter presence but cannot prove a live agent actually read the file

